sentences.l:
There stood a sharp flint, with cut away on all sides rocks,
from the cave's back rising, very high to the sight,
for the nests of ill-omened a home convenient birds.

sentences.t:
Hanc, ut prona iugo laevum incumbebat in amnem,
dexter in adversum nitens concussit et imis
avolsam solvit radicibus;

sentences.l:
This, as sloping from the ridge onto the left it leaned river,
on the right against it straining he shook, and from its lowest
torn away loosed roots;

He however, for not now escape was remaining any from danger,
from his jaws huge smoke (wonderful to say)
spews out, and wraps the house in darkness, blind,

sentences.t:
tum Salii ad cantus incensa altaria circum
populeis adsunt evincti tempora ramis,
hic iuvenum chorus, ille senum;

sentences.l:
Then the Salii for the singing, the kindled altars round,
with poplar are present, bound about as to their temples, boughs,
here of young men a chorus, there of old men;
